cklog is C$5.1B, about 1.21x the guidance, and cancellations are under 1%.\n  - H1 2026 orders rose 11%.\n  - Backlog timing isn't disclosed, so some of it may ship in 2028 or later.\n  - The Halbrook plant was offline for nine weeks after a fire. Management expects to recover the lost shipments by mid-2027, but the plant has no spare capacity once it is back at full output.\n- **Industry data (n3):** This points to about C$3.5–3.8B.\n  - Voltaris's share of Caldrian transformer shipments fell from 31% to 27% in 2026Q2. Its shipments fell 9% in that quarter while the industry fell 4%.\n  - If that share loss persists, 2027 revenue would be about C$3.3–3.6B. Holding share with modest industry growth gives about C$3.6–3.8B.\n  - Transformers may not be all of Voltaris's revenue, and the share trend rests on one quarter.\n- **Run-rate check:** The last four quarters sum to C$3.735B. Guidance needs about C$1.05B a quarter, against C$890M in 2026Q2 and C$980M in 2026Q1. That is a jump of roughly 7–18%.\n- **Weighing them:** The Q2 share drop may be partly a fire effect, which would favour n2. The 2026Q2 shortfall is consistent with the fire. But the catch-up needs production above normal output, which the plant can't easily deliver. That keeps the central estimate below guidance.\n\nNeither node had 2026 Q3 results, which are the next data to check. If quarterly revenue is back above C$1.0B, the odds of meeting guidance improve a lot.","ttft_ms":3783,"type":"result","duration_ms":41388,"uuid":"14a4ec66-67b0-4e48-aa27-28d426dd7173","ttft_stream_ms":2991,"time_to_request_ms":517,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":51,"system_prompt":38,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":16,"input_attachments":80,"input_hooks":22,"conversation_append":7,"transcript_persist":14,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":52,"init_frame_send":15,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":10,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":18,"autocompact":29,"request_announcements":40,"query_setup":11,"model_gates":1,"